{"collectors": ["execution_timeline", "binding_cost", "collective_calibration", "nccl_tuning"], "requested_fields": ["execution_timeline.per_device_intervals_ms", "execution_timeline.cpu_to_cuda_submit_associations", "execution_timeline.clock_alignment_bounds", "execution_timeline.synchronization_events", "execution_timeline.gradient_post_accumulate_callback_costs_ms", "binding_cost.parent_whole_invocation_ms", "binding_cost.binding_only_passthrough_ms", "binding_cost.ab_ba_worker_costs", "binding_cost.quality_check_results", "collective_calibration.allreduce_sum_f32_28351488B_ms", "collective_calibration.allreduce_sum_f32_157541376B_ms", "collective_calibration.warmed_worker_correctness_results", "nccl_tuning.algorithm_per_observed_size", "nccl_tuning.protocol_per_observed_size", "nccl_tuning.channels_per_observed_size", "nccl_tuning.transport_decisions"], "unavailable_fields": {"per_aggregate_wire_transfer_ms": "NCCL kernel durations include device waiting (parent trace: sequence 21 runs 114.43 ms on rank 0 vs 3.59 ms on rank 1 for the identical 28351488-byte allreduce); no available collector separates waiting from wire transfer, and nsys timelines cannot either", "per_aggregate_pcie_nvlink_bytes": "Hardware counters require a successful collector-specific probe; capability probe left pcie_bytes/nvlink_bytes unknown, peer_access is 0 in both directions with SHM/direct/direct channels, and device_telemetry supplies device-wide NVML rates with native windows only - traffic must not be invented from logical payload sizes", "exact_bucket_to_collective_identity": "Each of the 12 equal-size 28351488-byte allreduces carries 12 bucket_candidates; exact links require native correlation plus observed gradient-storage membership, so ambiguous candidates must be retained", "nccl_tuning.clean_per_collective_timing": "nccl_tuning does not join payload-size matches to operator groups or supply clean timing; the warmed synthetic timing reference is collective_calibration instead", "gpu_ready_and_consumer_completion_times": "execution_timeline reports clock alignment bounds for CPU submissions only; GPU readiness and consumer completion may remain unknown", "clean_host_dispatch_costs": "python_runtime was not selected; its cProfile inclusive/self times perturb execution and are not clean performance scores or GPU compute durations"}, "rationale": "All three sync_wait_budget_ms candidates reduced the objective (max-rank communication_kernel_sum_ms 94.49 -> 71.35 at 250 ms, 76.65 at 500 ms, 86.97 at 2000 ms) while every one violated the step_ms constraint (227.04/276.86/264.36 vs limit 151.86, original reference 144.63), so decision was no_valid_parameter_candidate. Select the Pareto-best revision 560d64a468acf7c63d3e5eee7f714a24dd8b3ad869c9e5b8ee98a7df04b4ab44 (sync_wait_budget_ms=250: lowest step_ms and lowest objective) and resolve two uncertainties. (1) Attribution of the +82 ms step regression: it must not be assumed to be algorithm cost - the comm-sum rank asymmetry flips sign across budgets (500 ms: rank0 76.6 > rank1 64.0; 2000 ms: rank1 87.0 > rank0 60.2; 250 ms: rank1 71.3 > rank0 61.0) and the parent trace shows waiting-dominated kernels, so execution_timeline is requested for per-device intervals, CPU-to-CUDA submit associations, synchronization events and passive post-accumulate callbacks (CPU clock bounds only), and binding_cost is requested because the additive legacy binding (functional_sites 2, framework_fallbacks 0) could itself account for whole-invocation cost via clean AB/BA parent-vs-passthrough; reference invocations (13/13 coverage) may be verification or composition, not fallback. (2) Headroom of the communication objective itself: collective_calibration gives a warmed synthetic full-world SUM allreduce reference at the actually observed sizes (12 x 28351488 B f32 plus 1 x 157541376 B f32) with correctness checks to separate intrinsic SHM-fabric cost from arrival-skew waiting (a reference experiment, not a lower bound or critical-path estimate), and nccl_tuning records the actual NCCL algorithm/protocol/channel decisions at those sizes since kernel entry names alone (RING_LL) do not identify the protocol. Excluded: torch (already ran - observations.json and per-candidate communication_kernel_sum_ms exist), nsys (cannot separate NCCL waiting from wire transfer nor prove bucket identity; attribution is covered by execution_timeline), device_telemetry (device-wide NVML rates with native windows, no per-collective attribution; peer_access 0), python_runtime (perturbs execution; host dispatch not yet implicated by evidence), candidate_diagnostics (no capability or trace evidence describes its outputs).", "revision": "560d64a468acf7c63d3e5eee7f714a24dd8b3ad869c9e5b8ee98a7df04b4ab44"}
